From d5733f56becb52b2a3ef873854f7326495f87753 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yashgix <125082291+yashgix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:39:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Send OpenAPI and ctx.fetch queries exactly as built

The invocation fetch read each query into parameters and sent it again form-encoded, which escaped list commas, slashes and colons and turned percent-encoded spaces into plus signs. The request now keeps its query as written, without its fragment. The OpenAPI builder escapes only what a URI query cannot hold and refuses a reserved value containing a number sign.

Release-note: Fix: OpenAPI tools and app requests now send query strings exactly as built, so comma separated lists and encoded spaces reach the API unchanged.
